					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Microsoft Office 2016 (Machine) -&gt; Security Settings -&gt; IE Security "Block popups" is set to "Enabled" and 'pptview.exe' is checked.

Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: 

HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Internet Explorer\Main\FeatureControl\FEATURE_WEBOC_POPUPMANAGEMENT

Criteria: If the value pptview.exe is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding.
</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Fix_Text</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Microsoft Office 2016 (Machine) -&gt; Security Settings -&gt; IE Security "Block popups" to "Enabled" and place a check in the 'pptview.exe' check box.
</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
