					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Check_Content</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Microsoft Office 2016 (Machine) -&gt; Security Settings -&gt; IE Security "Add-on Management" is set to "Enabled" and 'excel.exe' is checked.

Procedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: 

HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Internet Explorer\Main\FeatureControl\FEATURE_ADDON_MANAGEMENT

Criteria: If the value excel.exe is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Fix_Text</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Set the policy value for Computer Configuration -&gt; Administrative Templates -&gt; Microsoft Office 2016 (Machine) -&gt; Security Settings -&gt; IE Security "Add-on Management" to "Enabled" and place a check in the 'excel.exe' check box.
</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
